            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0704" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg602"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/714: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-05T12:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1919,
                                noon.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 6,
                            2.20 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2673. Department’s 2022 March 3, 5 p.m.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d574-f1"/> Embassy
                    has received today note signed by Under Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs
                    accepting Siberian Railway plan. Note dated March 4th reads: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In reply to the note of February 12th ultimo<anchor n="23"
                                xml:id="d574-f2"/> I have the honor to inform Your Excellency that
                            the Royal Government has adhered to the plan of the Imperial Government
                            of Japan for the control of the Eastern Chinese [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Chinese Eastern</hi>] and Trans-Siberian Railways in the zone of
                            operation of the Allied military forces with the financial reservations
                            made by the Government of the United States and with the same
                            interpretation of the word ‘interests’ desired by the American
                            Government.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
